            <ArticleTitle>[Long-term-treatment of chronic pain patients with flupirtine--on hepatotoxicity and persistent effectiveness from 7 months to 22 years].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-34</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">After an extended series of investigations in animals, healthy volunteers and pain patients with different methods, flupirtine was introduced in 1986 into the German market. Flupirtine has a unique chemical structure and differs in its profile of effects and side effects from established NSAIDs (non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs) on the one hand and from opioids on the other hand. In the years after introduction, muscle relaxing effects were observed and experimentally shown. They were therapeutically utilized in tension-associated pain. Evidence of the efficacy in acute and chronic musculoskeletal pain syndromes was verified in many controlled and in open studies.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Experience report and case presentation</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The report in this paper of long-term treatment of chronic pain patients from 7 months to 22 years principally confirms its persistent effectiveness and tolerability. Tiredness and dizziness are frequent side effects. Flupirtine-associated hepatotoxicities are rare events.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">For pain patients for which NSAIDs or opioids are contraindicated or in appropriate, flupirtine is a necessary option.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
